&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The community you will join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is seeking a Legal Intern to join the Brazil legal consulting and Litigation teams for a 24-month internship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb’s legal team embodies the company’s innovative and entrepreneurial spirit. At the frontier of the sharing economy, Airbnb is breaking new ground in matters of policy and law around the world. Where some see obstacles, we see opportunities to find creative and practical solutions. We’re an adventurous, fast-moving group. This internship is right for you if you are a law student (bachelor) with a proactive attitude, strong organization skills, willingness to learn, and embrace adventures in a fast paced environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to supporting students from underrepresented backgrounds in law and tech. We are looking for candidates who identify as black and highly encourage them to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The difference you will make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern, you’ll be integrated into a team where you’ll contribute to challenging projects. Your manager, team, and our incredible employee community will strive to be superhosts to you. We provide the support, mentorship, fun, and real world experience needed to accelerate your learning and make a real impact on our product, as Airbnb revolutionizes connection, belonging, and travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your assigned projects will depend on the department’s needs and your interests. You will have the opportunity to work closely with the Litigation team of Airbnb Brazil to support a variety of litigation functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A typical day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The intern will support the Brazil Litigation team in:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing summonings from judicial and administrative cases and extrajudicial notices;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring judicial and administrative cases, gathering data to support Airbnb&#39;s defenses and updating Airbnb&#39;s internal systems with information about judicial and administrative cases;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing outside counsel work and consumer litigation cases;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drafting reports and responses to judicial and administrative requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating on the Litigation Team&#39;s projects, besides collaborating on daily basis workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current second or third year law school student&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in the English language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpersonal skills with an interest in building relationships and collaborating across the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable and able to adjust plans and manage changes effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to prioritize tasks, meet deadlines, and handle multiple projects simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in learning about in-house legal practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in the litigation practice is a plus but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of this position, the successful applicant will need to be based in São Paulo for in-person meetings and collaboration. Additionally, you must have work authorization for Brazil to be eligible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our commitment to inclusion &amp;amp; belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the best and brightest people from the broadest talent pool possible. We believe a diversity of ideas fosters innovation and engagement, and allows us to attract the best people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. If you need assistance, or a reasonable accommodation during the application and recruiting process, please contact us at: &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&quot;&gt;reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please submit all application materials in English.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career or degree level. The base pay range shown below is monthly, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Brazil Monthly Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;R$3.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;R$3.000 BRL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No global movement springs from individuals. It takes an entire team united behind something big. Airbnb helps anyone belong anywhere as the world’s largest community-driven hospitality company. Every day, we connect thousands of guests and hosts online, leading to meaningful experiences in the real world. We’re helping people live like locals in parts unknown while breaking down cultural barriers and bringing people together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you wake up everyday asking yourself how you can impact the creation of a truly local experience that delights global users? Do you love working with content, design, marketing and engineering teams? Do you want to be part of one of the teams that is actively working on bringing to life Airbnb’s mission, where everyone can belong anywhere? Do you love to work in a fast-paced, fun, fast-growing company? Do you like to work in a multicultural team? Do you love owning the localization strategy for your market?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you answered yes to all the questions above, we would love to talk to you, as the Localization team at Airbnb is looking for an experienced Localization Manager, Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is expecting the biggest travel rebound of the century with COVID receding world wide and fully reopening cross-border travel. Airbnb has been reinventing itself as a consequence of IPO and the post pandemic world. Airbnb Marketing and Product strategy has evolved and is becoming more sophisticated and demanding. As a consequence the Localization team has been growing fast with the company and steadily evolving and increasing our scope, impact and influence.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Airbnb, Localization has transformed from traditional translation management into a key driver of international growth. Our team partners with launching teams across all content, spearheading complex core product capabilities like the Translation Engine—a specialized machine translation service tailored for user-generated content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Localization Manager, you will be pivotal in our international expansion efforts, a top priority for Airbnb. You will join the core leadership team in your region, shaping local initiatives and adapting global strategies to meet market needs. Your role will encompass not only driving language strategy but also fostering collaboration with internal stakeholders and external partners to create internationalized products that resonate with local audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Localization Managers serve as the linguistic and cultural expert in collaborating with local teams to develop strategy to drive business growth - adapting and developing product and services that meet local needs. You are the guardians of Airbnb’s tone, style, and voice, and the enforcers of quality and excellence in their languages. As a Localization Manager, you&#39;re not only passionate about languages and cultures, but also about giving our users a native experience across all platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to shape the world of the sharing economy - Airbnb is the place to be. We work hard, we laugh a lot, we brainstorm nonstop, and we give the best high-fives in town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb’s Localization Manager role and responsibility goes beyond the traditional focus of ensuring quality of translated content:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Country Manager, Marketing Manager, Legal Counsel, Business Operations, Policy and Communications Manager to devise business strategies that align with Airbnb’s goals in your market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to being the linguistic and cultural expert for the region/market, proactively share roadmap and intent behind product updates to utilize and adopt global strategy to the target market&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and understand market expectations, crafting language strategies that offer users an authentic native experience in Canada&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide linguistic and cultural expertise in developing strategy to drive international growth, proactively influencing stakeholders to deliver the best possible user experience to the global community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive localization of Product naming and Creative copies, engaging and representing local teams to build Airbnb’s brand in international markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate and drive conversations with central and local teams to influence product changes to support market needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively research the needs of Airbnb international users in collaboration with Consumer Insights and Research team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand challenges in the localization process and lead localization quality improvement initiatives at the language and team level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of the strategy to help achieve excellence in localization quality across all platforms&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure translation and QA vendors deliver high quality service that align with Airbnb’s standards. Assess vendor metrics to identify issues or trends, and drive improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate language feedback from both users and Airbnb employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain linguistic and cultural standards and guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support content copywriting for marketing initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Localization Program Managers and Linguistic QA Managers to ensure we ship top quality products internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in product localization with a proven track record of owning localization strategy in international launches addition to managing language quality and content localization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and native knowledge of Canadian French is a must&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building market strategies informed by thorough market research and data analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong capability to collaborate across functions, driving partnerships, and initiatives forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to show initiative and work independently, and drive initiatives at a strategic level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding experience in project/program management, partner/stakeholder management, with experience working across cross-functional teams and time-zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent ability to manage multiple and diverse stakeholders across businesses and leadership levels with excellent communication/presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of being a self-starter, self-motivated and outcome-oriented individual who seeks ownership and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work at both strategic and tactical levels, with a proven track record to execute in ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to prioritize and manage conflicting demands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Please submit your resume/CV in English*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;This position is Canada - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a province where Airbnb Canada, Inc. has a registered entity. Currently we can hire in the following provinces: Ontario, British Columbia, Quebec, and Saskatchewan. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with your recruiter on what provinces you are eligible to work from.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to also provide a disability inclusive application and interview process. If you are a candidate with a disability and require reasonable accommodation in order to submit an application, please contact us at: reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com. Please include your full name, the role you’re applying for and the accommodation necessary to assist you with the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We ask that you only reach out to us if you are a candidate whose disability prevents you from being able to complete our online application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We use automated tools to help our recruiting team efficiently screen a large volume of applications. All final hiring decisions are made by a human reviewer.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;This role is newly created and does not replace or backfill an existing position.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Canada Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$91,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$107,000 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Airbnb a pris le jour en 2007 lorsque deux Hôtes ont accueilli trois invités dans leur maison de San Francisco, et compte depuis lors plus de 4 millions d&#39;Hôtes qui ont accueilli plus d&#39;un milliard d&#39;invités dans presque tous les pays du monde. Chaque jour, les Hôtes proposent des séjours et des expériences uniques qui permettent aux invités de se connecter de manière plus authentique aux communautés.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;La communauté que vous rejoindrez :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Personne ne peut lancer un mouvement mondial tout seul. Il faut toute une équipe pour réaliser de grandes choses. Airbnb aide tout le monde à se sentir chez soi, partout. C&#39;est la plus grande entreprise d&#39;hébergement au monde axée sur la communauté. Chaque jour, on connecte des milliers de voyageurs et d&#39;hôtes en ligne, ce qui nous permet de faire vivre des expériences significatives dans le monde réel. On aide les gens à vivre comme des gens du coin dans des endroits inconnus tout en brisant les barrières culturelles et en rassemblant le monde.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous vous réveillez tous les matins en vous demandant comment vous pouvez contribuer à la création d&#39;une expérience vraiment locale qui ravira les utilisateurs du monde entier? Aimez-vous travailler avec des équipes techniques, de contenu, de conception et de marketing? Voulez-vous faire partie de l&#39;une des équipes qui travaillent activement à donner vie à la mission d&#39;Airbnb, où chacun peut se sentir chez soi, ailleurs? Aimez-vous travailler dans une entreprise dynamique et en pleine croissance où on a du plaisir? Aimez-vous travailler dans une équipe multiculturelle? Aimez-vous être responsable de la stratégie de localisation pour votre marché?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Si vous avez répondu oui à toutes les questions ci-dessus, on est intéressés. L&#39;équipe de localisation d&#39;Airbnb est à la recherche d&#39;un·e responsable de la localisation d&#39;expérience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;La différence que vous ferez :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb s&#39;attend à la plus grosse reprise des voyages du siècle avec la fin de la pandémie de COVID-19 dans le monde et la réouverture complète des voyages internationaux. Airbnb se réinvente en raison de son introduction en bourse et du monde post-pandémique. La stratégie marketing et produit d&#39;Airbnb a évolué et devient de plus en plus sophistiquée et exigeante. En conséquence, l&#39;équipe de localisation a grandi rapidement avec l&#39;entreprise et a constamment évolué et augmenté notre portée, notre impact et notre influence.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Airbnb, la localisation est passée de la gestion traditionnelle de la traduction à un moteur clé de la croissance internationale. Notre équipe collabore avec les équipes de lancement pour tous les contenus, en lançant des fonctionnalités de produits de base complexes comme le Translation Engine, un service de traduction automatique spécialisé adapté au contenu généré par les utilisateurs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que responsable de la localisation, vous jouerez un rôle central dans nos efforts d&#39;expansion internationale, une priorité absolue pour Airbnb. Vous rejoindrez l&#39;équipe de direction principale de votre région, façonnant les initiatives locales et adaptant les stratégies mondiales pour répondre aux besoins du marché. Votre rôle consistera non seulement à piloter la stratégie linguistique, mais aussi à favoriser la collaboration avec les parties prenantes internes et les partenaires externes pour créer des produits internationalisés qui sont bien adaptés aux publics locaux.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Les responsables de la localisation agissent en tant qu&#39;experts linguistiques et culturels en collaborant avec les équipes locales pour élaborer une stratégie visant à stimuler la croissance de l&#39;entreprise, en adaptant et en développant des produits et des services qui répondent aux besoins locaux. Vous devez porter le ton, le style et la voix d&#39;Airbnb, ainsi que garantir la qualité et l&#39;excellence dans votre langue. En tant que responsable de la localisation, vous êtes non seulement passionné·e par les langues et les cultures, mais aussi par l&#39;idée d&#39;offrir à nos utilisateurs une expérience native sur toutes les plateformes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Si vous voulez façonner le monde de l&#39;économie de partage, Airbnb est l&#39;endroit idéal. On travaille dur, on rit beaucoup, on échange sans arrêt et on vit ensemble des moments inoubliables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une journée typique :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le rôle et la responsabilité du responsable de la localisation d&#39;Airbnb vont au-delà de l&#39;objectif traditionnel d&#39;assurer la qualité du contenu traduit:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travailler en étroite collaboration avec le directeur national, le directeur du marketing, le conseiller juridique, le directeur des opérations commerciales, des politiques et des communications pour élaborer des stratégies commerciales qui s&#39;alignent aux objectifs d&#39;Airbnb sur votre marché.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;En plus d&#39;être l&#39;expert·e linguistique et culturel·le de la région ou du marché, partager de manière proactive la feuille de route et le but derrière les mises à jour de produits pour utiliser et adopter la stratégie mondiale dans le marché cible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifier et comprendre les attentes du marché en élaborant des stratégies linguistiques qui offrent aux utilisateurs une expérience authentique au Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fournir une expertise linguistique et culturelle dans l&#39;élaboration d&#39;une stratégie pour stimuler la croissance internationale, en influençant de manière proactive les parties prenantes pour offrir la meilleure expérience utilisateur possible à la communauté mondiale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mener et diriger la localisation des noms de produits et des textes créatifs en impliquant et en représentant les équipes locales pour bien établir la marque Airbnb sur les marchés internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lancer et mener des conversations avec les équipes centrales et locales pour influencer les changements de produits afin de répondre aux besoins du marché.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chercher activement à connaître les besoins des utilisateurs internationaux d&#39;Airbnb en collaboration avec l&#39;équipe de recherche et d&#39;analyse des consommateurs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprendre les défis du processus de localisation et diriger les initiatives d&#39;amélioration de la qualité de la localisation au niveau de la langue et de l&#39;équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimiser la stratégie pour atteindre l&#39;excellence en matière de qualité de localisation sur toutes les plateformes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;S&#39;assurer que les fournisseurs de traduction et d&#39;assurance qualité offrent un service de haute qualité conforme aux standards d&#39;Airbnb. Évaluer les indicateurs des fournisseurs pour identifier les problèmes ou les tendances et apporter des améliorations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordonner les remarques linguistiques des utilisateurs et des employés d&#39;Airbnb.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Élaborer et maintenir des standards et des lignes directrices linguistiques et culturelles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer à la rédaction de contenu pour les initiatives de marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travailler avec les responsables des programmes de localisation et les responsables de l&#39;assurance qualité linguistique pour s&#39;assurer qu&#39;on offre des produits de qualité supérieure à l&#39;international.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Votre expertise :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus de 8&amp;nbsp;ans d&#39;expérience en localisation de produits avec une expérience avérée en stratégie de localisation dans les lancements internationaux, ainsi qu&#39;en gestion de la qualité linguistique et de la localisation de contenu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise de l&#39;anglais et connaissance du français canadien (langue maternelle) obligatoire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience dans l&#39;élaboration de stratégies de marché fondées sur des études de marché approfondies et l&#39;analyse de données.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forte capacité à collaborer entre les fonctions et à faire avancer les partenariats et les initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à faire preuve d&#39;initiative et à travailler de manière autonome, ainsi qu&#39;à mener des initiatives à un niveau stratégique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience exceptionnelle en gestion de projet et de programme, en gestion de partenaires et de parties prenantes, avec une expérience de travail au sein d&#39;équipes interfonctionnelles dans différents fuseaux horaires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellente capacité à gérer de multiples et diverses parties prenantes à travers les entreprises et les niveaux de direction avec d&#39;excellentes compétences en communication et en présentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience démontrant une capacité à prendre des initiatives, à se motiver, à obtenir des résultats et à assumer ses responsabilités.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à travailler à la fois aux niveaux stratégique et tactique, avec une expérience avérée de la mise en œuvre dans des environnements complexes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à établir des priorités et à gérer des demandes contradictoires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Envoyez votre resume/CV en anglais*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Votre emplacement :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En raison de la nature de ce poste, le candidat retenu devra être basé au Canada pour pouvoir effectuer son travail. Actuellement, les employés peuvent être situés dans : la Colombie-Britannique, l’Ontario, le Québec, l’Alberta ou le Saskatchewan. Cette liste est continuellement mise à jour, veuillez vérifier avec nous si les provinces dans lesquelles vous vivez figurent sur la liste. Si votre poste est employé par une autre entité Airbnb, votre recruteur vous informera des provinces dans lesquelles vous êtes éligible pour travailler.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notre engagement envers l’inclusion et l’appartenance :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb s&#39;engage à travailler avec le vivier de talents le plus large possible. Nous pensons que la diversité des idées favorise l’innovation et l’engagement, et nous permet d’attirer des personnes créatives et de développer les meilleurs produits, services et solutions. Toutes les personnes qualifiées sont encouragées à postuler.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous nous efforçons également de proposer un processus de candidature et d&#39;entretien inclusif pour les personnes handicapées. Si vous êtes un candidat handicapé et avez besoin d&#39;aménagements raisonnables pour soumettre une candidature, veuillez nous contacter à l&#39;adresse : raisonnableaccommodations@airbnb.com. Veuillez inclure votre nom complet, le poste pour lequel vous postulez et les aménagements nécessaires pour vous aider dans le processus de recrutement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous vous demandons de nous contacter uniquement si vous êtes un candidat dont le handicap vous empêche de remplir notre candidature en ligne.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nous utilisons des outils automatisés pour aider notre équipe de recrutement à examiner efficacement un grand nombre de candidatures. Toutes les décisions finales d’embauche sont prises par une personne humaine.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ce poste est nouvellement créé et ne remplace ni ne pourvoit un poste existant.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Canada Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$91,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$107,000 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Machine Learning and Artificial Intelligence are at the heart of the Airbnb product. From Trust to Payments, and from Customer Service to Marketing we rely on ML to ensure that guests and hosts have the best possible experience with Airbnb.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Community Support Products (CSP) Machine Learning team is the core team responsible for driving CSxAI (Customer Support x Artificial Intelligence) initiatives by adopting the Generative AI technologies to enable an intelligent, scalable and exceptional service experience. The team develops and enhances various AI models, ML services and tools including LLM fine-tuning and optimization, RAG/Search,&amp;nbsp; LLM evaluation and testing automation, feedback-based learning and guardrail for a wide range of applications in Airbnb.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The richness of Airbnb&#39;s data, the complexity of its marketplace and the variety innate in our product mean that we need to operate at the state of the art of AI practice. We are committed to investing in long&amp;nbsp;term innovation to solve the complex problems we face, and to do that we need the very best experts in ML and AI to join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe our current customer experiences in these domains are only scratching the surface of the innovations that are possible, and that science is at the heart of delivering a step-function change for our Guest and and Host on Airbnb.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build and leverage cutting edge AI technologies to transform Airbnb’s customer service by delivering personalized, easy-to-use and proactive customer service experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Many of the initiatives you’ll tackle are in their early conceptual stages. You will have the opportunity to shape these ideas from inception to production, turning visionary concepts into impactful realities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Envision, champion, and support the development of novel ML systems, product integrations, and performance optimizations to solve real-world problems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work cross-functionally with product, design, and other engineering counterparts to design and build efficient AI solutions for Airbnb CS products&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn and share the latest AI/ML technologies with the team across regions( China and the US).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD/Master’s degree, preferably in CS, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years of ML engineering experience, with ownership responsibility over large-scale software systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in the design and development of AI and ML systems and services, and a deep passion for building efficient and scalable ML-powered products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with LLM driven chatbot and Agentic AI products would be a big plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and the ability to work well within a team and with teams across the engineering, product &amp;amp; design organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluency in both English and Mandarin is essential.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is China - Remote Eligible&lt;/strong&gt;. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. Your recruiter will inform you what cities you are able to work from depending on your personal legal working identity and Airbnb internal policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Airbnb Hotels team is a fun, fast-growing group leading Airbnb’s expansion into the hotel sector. Operating with an entrepreneurial spirit, this team combines the simplicity, product excellence, and guest-centered ethos that define Airbnb. This team’s mission is to deliver the smoothest, most intuitive hotel booking experience for guests, while helping hotels easily drive incremental bookings so they can focus on delivering the best hospitality. The ultimate aim is to help more people discover high-quality hotels, creating value for guests and our hotel partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Manager, Connectivity Partner, you will be responsible for managing and executing strategy to the overall Hotels Connectivity. You will develop and lead a high-performing team responsible for the relationship management, enablement, and performance management of Airbnb’s Connectivity partners (i.e Channel managers, CRS and PMS systems). These connectivities enable real-time inventory updates, automated reservation delivery, and improved visibility, allowing hotels to drive bookings. This role will be accountable for helping grow Airbnb’s business through software partners. You will be responsible for setting up team and strategies, exceeding quarterly business and technical KPIs, establishing world-class account management practices, and mentoring and motivating your team members. You will be reporting to the Senior Manager, Global Enterprise and Connectivity Partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage distributed team of Connectivity Partner Managers and Specialists and assist in partner management and new business development for supply acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for the team to meet and exceed quarterly revenue, supply acquisition goals and other OKRs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a global strategy playbook, working closely with a distributed team of Connectivity Partners. Work closely with the Homes Connectivity team business as well.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create operational rhythm, establish and track KPIs, analyze business growth and other key metrics to identify trends, drive new business opportunities, and ensure resolution of business challenges with a sense of urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain successful business practices for managing strategic connectivity partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive success with strategic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor business needs and work closely with Product, Technical Support, and Account Management and Sales Leadership to help drive feature adoption and business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as primary Airbnb point of contact for all internal questions, escalations and service improvements regarding connectivity partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional experience working in sales/account management roles - tourism, e-commerce, and hospitality is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years experience managing and leading highly effective teams with proven track record of meeting and exceeding goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven to contribute and drive solutions to hotels supply acquisition and revenue goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly motivated and engaged team builder with ability to coach and mentor Connectivity team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and driving channel sales and marketing initiatives in collaboration with Connectivity team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop a strategy, communicate it clearly and get buy-in and support to execute against quarterly goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills to identify opportunities, operationalize execution, and drive business results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence senior Airbnb leadership level or within partners leadership teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work within a matrix, solve problems and influence cross-functional teams; strong stakeholder management across the organization, working with Marketing, Product, Technology, Legal, FP&amp;amp;A, regional field teams (Sales and Account Management) and enterprise account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the hospitality technology space, knowledge of OTA, channel managers and/or Property management systems, and experience with API integrations strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with CRM tools (Salesforce), project management, and business intelligence tools (Tableau)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel as needed to meet team members and engage with partners and customers at industry events. May be up to 50% of time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a state where Airbnb, Inc. has a registered entity. &lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://careers.airbnb.com/&quot;&gt;Click here for the up-to-date list of excluded states. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with us if the state you live in is on the exclusion list&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;If your position is employed by another Airbnb entity, your recruiter will inform you what states you are eligible to work from.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
